==English==

===Etymology===
Probably {{bor+|en|yi|גליטש|nocap=1}}, from {{der|en|de|glitschig||slippy}}, from {{m|de|glitschen|t=to slide, glide, slip}} + {{m|de|-ig||-y}}. Related to {{m|de|gleiten||glide}}. Cognate with {{cog|fr|glisser||to slip, slide, skid}}.

Popularized in the 1960s, by the US space program. Attested in 1962 by American astronaut {{w|John Glenn}}, in reference to spikes in electrical current.<ref name="moradi">Moradi, Iman. (2004) [https://web.archive.org/web/20050105115656/http://oculasm.org/glitch/download/Glitch_dissertation_print_with_pics.pdf Glitch Aesthetic]</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɡlɪt͡ʃ/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-glitch.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{hyph|en|glitch}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪtʃ|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[problem]] affecting [[function]].
#: {{syn|en|bug|hitch|imperfection|quirk|gremlin}}
#: {{ux|en|They are still trying to work out all the '''glitches'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1965|work=Time magazine|passage='''Glitches'''—a spaceman’s word for irritating disturbances.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|year=1999|actor=Carrie-Anne Moss|title=The Matrix|medium=motion picture|writers=The Wachowski Brothers|role=Trinity|passage=A déjà vu is usually a '''glitch''' in the Matrix. It happens when they change something.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|title=Foodpanda faces backlash after calling Thai protest 'terrorism'|text=Some claimed on Monday that Foodpanda's account deletion system reported being under maintenance and could not process their request. It is unclear if the flock of requests had created a system failure, or Foodpanda had cut access on purpose, or the timing was merely a coincidence. The '''glitch''' only added fuel to online sympathizers' outrage.|url=https://asia.nikkei.com/Business/Food-Beverage/Foodpanda-faces-backlash-after-calling-Thai-protest-terrorism|date=2021-07-20|accessdate=2021-07-20|work=Nikkei Asia|publisher=Nikkei Inc|author=Masayuki Yuda}}
# {{lb|en|countable|informal|engineering}} An unexpected behavior in an electrical [[signal]], especially if the signal spontaneously returns to expected behavior after a period of time.
#: {{cot|en|surge|spike|instability}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1962|author=w:John Glenn|title=Into Orbit|publisher=Cassell|location=London    |passage=Another term we adopted to describe some of our problems was "'''glitch'''." Literally, a '''glitch''' is a spike or change in voltage in an electrical circuit which takes place when the circuit suddenly has a new load put on it. You have probably noticed a dimming of lights in your home when you turn a switch or start the dryer or the television set.}}
# {{lb|en|video games}} A [[bug]] or an [[exploit]].
#: {{ux|en|Performing this '''glitch''' gives you extra lives.}}
#* {{quote-web
|en
|date=September 4, 2021
|author=Paarnahkrin
|title=8.550 War Assets - How to achieve the highest possible score
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20211207052620/https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2582083059
|archivedate=07 December 2021
|url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2582083059
|work=w:Steam Community
|section=Paarnahkrin's Guides
|url2=https://archive.ph/6IYTS
|text=How to reach 8.555 ー The '''glitch'''<br>You need to have {{w|Urdnot Wrex|Wrex}} alive and sabotage the cure. Without the '''glitch''', Wrex will discover the lie and try to kill you after Priority: Citadel II when you try to go back to the {{w|Normandy (Mass Effect)|Normandy}}. Triggering this scene will remove Wrex and the Clan Urdnot in the war assets list<br>The '''glitch''' is easy, when you want to leave the {{w|Citadel (Mass Effect)|Citadel}}, simply go to a fast travel shuttle, then in a DLC area (Dr. Bryson's Lab or Silversun Strip)<br>Then again the shuttle, and go back to the Normandy from here}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable|music genre}} A [[genre]] of [[experimental]] [[electronic music]] since the 1990s, characterized by a deliberate use of [[sonic]] [[artifact]]s that would normally be viewed as [[unwanted]] [[noise]].
#: {{hyper|en|electronic music}}
