|passage=Previous theorists have often tried to test whether visual space is best described by a small set of traditional '''geometries''', such as the Euclidean '''geometry''' most of us studied in High School or the hyperbolic and spherical '''geometries''' introduced by 19<sup>th</sup>-century mathematicians.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} The observed or specified spatial attributes of an object, etc.
