{{en-adj|more,er}}

# Made of, or relating to, [[gold]]. {{C|en|Gold}}
#: {{ux|en|She wore a '''golden''' crown.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1749|author=Henry Fielding|title=The History of Tom Jones, a Foundling|passage=And now the concern which Partridge felt at being obliged to quit the warm chimney-corner, and a cup of excellent liquor, was somewhat compensated by hearing that he was to proceed no farther on foot, for Jones, by '''golden''' arguments, had prevailed with the boy to attend him back to the inn whither he had before conducted Sophia {{...}}}}
# Having a [[color]] or other [[richness]] [[suggestive]] of gold.
#: {{ux|en|Under a '''golden''' sun.}}
#: {{color panel|E3AF05}}
# Of a [[beverage]], [[flavoured]] or [[colored]] with [[turmeric]]. {{defdate|from c. 2010}}
# Marked by [[prosperity]], [[creativity]] etc.
#: {{ux|en|The Renaissance was a '''golden''' era.}}
#: {{co|en|the [[Golden Horseshoe]]}}
#* {{RQ:Fielding Tom Jones|passage=O Partridge! could I hope once again to see that face; but, alas! all those '''golden''' dreams are vanished for ever, and my only refuge from future misery is to forget the object of all my former happiness.}}
# [[advantageous|Advantageous]] or very [[favourable]].
#: {{ux|en|This is a [[golden opportunity|'''golden''' opportunity]]}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=October 20, 2011|author=Jamie Lillywhite|title=Tottenham 1 - 0 Rubin Kazan|work=BBC Sport|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/europe/15285221.stm
|passage=... a seasoned Champions League outfit, who beat Barcelona at the Nou Camp in 2009-10 and continually worked their way between the home defence to create some '''golden''' opportunities.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260927195941/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/europe/15285221.stm|archivedate=27 September 2026}}
# Relating to a fiftieth [[anniversary]].
#: {{ux|en|It's not long until our '''golden''' wedding.}}
# Relating to the [[elderly]] or [[retired]].
#: {{ux|en|After retiring, Bob and Judy moved to Arizona to live out their '''golden''' years.}}
# {{lb|en|UK|slang|predicative}} [[fine|Fine]], without [[problems]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=Colin Barr; Steve Katai|title=The Complete Idiot's Guide to Triathlon Training|publisher=Penguin|isbn=9781440625671|page=28
|passage=Many anti-fog variety goggles are available, but if you don&#39;t get that type, just rub a little spit on the lenses before you put them on in the water and you&#39;ll be '''golden'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=Mark Wiskup|title=Presentation S.O.S.: From Perspiration to Persuasion in 9 Easy Steps|publisher=Hachette UK|isbn=9780446568760
|passage=Therefore, the task ahead is easy. When the spotlight is on you, never let the audience down and you&#39;ll be '''golden'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Wayne R. Dempsey|title=101 Projects for Your Porsche Boxster|publisher=Motorbooks|isbn=9781610607957|page=68
|passage=If all of the marks line up perfectly, then you&#39;re '''golden''', and you can continue on with finishing up the installation.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|title=Grown Ups|lyricist=w:Jarvis Cocker|artist={{w|Pulp (band)|Pulp}}|album={{w|More (Pulp album)|More}}|year=2025|passage=I arrived pretty late, but you didn't seem to mind / We are not the first, but we are '''golden''' tonight}}

