==English==

===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|fr|glacial}}, from {{der|en|la|glaciālis}}, from {{m|la|glaciēs|t=ice}}. The sense "slow" refers to the speed of actual [[w:Glacier#Speed|glaciers]], typically around 1 meter per day.<ref>{{cite-book|year=2009|author=Amy Sterling Casil|title=The Creation of Canyons|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=czKDDwAAQBAJ&pg=PA8|isbn=9781615311286|page=8|publisher=The Rosen Publishing Group|1=en|passage=Glaciers are masses of highly compressed snow and ice that also flow downward in response to gravity, but much more slowly. This is the origin of the phrase “glacial speed.” If something is described as happening at glacial speed, that means it is occurring at a very slow pace.}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɡleɪ.sɪəl/|/ˈɡleɪ.ʃ(ɪ)əl/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-glacial.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪʃəl|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of, or relating to [[glacier]]s.
#: {{ux|en|We examined the '''glacial''' deposits.}}
#: ''Wang Shijin is a glacier expert and director of the Yulong Snow Mountain '''Glacial''' and Environmental Observation Research Station.'' [[File:Wang Shijin is a glacier expert.ogg]]
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Toyin Owoseje|title=Google marks Earth Day with doodle showing stark impacts of the climate crisis|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2022/04/22/world/earth-day-2022-google-doodle-climate-scli-intl|date=2022-04-22|passage=Users can see how a glacier at the summit of Mt. Kilimanjaro in Tanzania retreated between December 1986 and 2020, as well as '''glacial''' melt in Sermersooq, Greenland, between December 2000 and 2020.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220517221425/https://www.cnn.com/2022/04/22/world/earth-day-2022-google-doodle-climate-scli-intl/}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} Very [[slow]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1917|author=|title=Everybody's Magazine - Volume 37, Issue 2|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=zgNSAQAAMAAJ&q=%22glacial+speed%22|isbn=|page=56|publisher=Ridgeway Company|passage=He could remember a day that he had spent the whole of (he couldn't have been more than ten) running one of the great, creaking freight elevators at a '''glacial''' speed, answering the calls of the bell—one ring, five rings, three rings—with an almost unbearable sense of responsibility.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1953|author=United States. Congress. House. Committee on Armed Services|title=Defense Department Authorization and Oversight|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=hbwfAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA1251|isbn=|page=1251|publisher=U.S. Government Printing Office|passage=I understand that you commented that the Japanese are moving at '''glacial''' speed. This is not the only area where they are moving at '''glacial''' speed. They are moving at '''glacial''' speed in terms of trade barriers, and it is one thing that the American people recognize.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1999|author=Michael Goodchild; Max J. Egenhofer; Robin Fegeas; Cliff Kottman|title=Interoperating Geographic Information Systems|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=N_3JwJuN314C&pg=PA133|isbn=9780792384366|page=133|publisher=Springer Science & Business Media|passage=Paradoxically, then, the electronic speed offered by computer-based decision-making is often overwhelmed by the '''glacial''' speed of data reformatting and checking.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|writers={{w|Aline Brosh McKenna}}; {{w|Lauren Weisberger}}|title={{w|The Devil Wears Prada (film)|The Devil Wears Prada}}|year=2006|role=w:Miranda Priestly|actor=Meryl Streep|passage=By all means move at a '''glacial''' pace. You know how that thrills me.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=16 October 2010|title=Under the volcano|journal=w:The Economist|passage=Progress on judicial reform has been '''glacial''', meeting enormous resistance.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=John P. Kotter|title=Accelerate: Building Strategic Agility for a Faster-Moving World|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=RFzOAgAAQBAJ&pg=PA96|isbn=9781625272546|page=96|publisher=Harvard Business Review Press|passage=Lower-level people added front-line information that ordinarily wouldn't have made it up the hierarchy to the executive committee (or would have made it at '''glacial''' speed).}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Stuart E. Eizenstat|title=The Future of the Jews: How Global Forces are Impacting the Jewish People, Israel, and Its Relationship with the United States|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=AJ7_AwAAQBAJ&pg=PA105|isbn=9781442241763|page=105|publisher=Rowman & Littlefield|passage=The Gulf States and Saudi Arabia are modernizing but at a '''glacial''' speed in a world moving at digital speed.}}
# [[cold|Cold]] and [[icy]].
